[4.356, "o", "\r\n  source : Ultramarine Linux 44 (GNOME Edition) (Fedora, desktop: GNOME)\r\n  target : bluefin [ghcr.io/ublue-os/bluefin:stable] (Fedora, desktop: GNOME, backend: Bootc)\r\n  mode   : Hybrid\r\n\r\n  already in target image            2 package(s)\r\n  layer into system image            4 package(s)\r\n      cockpit  iptsd  libwacom-surface  libwacom-surface-data\r\n  Homebrew                           2 package(s)\r\n      neovim  ripgrep\r\n  Flatpak                            1 package(s)\r\n      vlc→org.videolan.VLC\r\n  skip                               2 package(s)\r\n\r\n  config files: 24 → /etc, 0 → toolbox, 0 → brew, 226 skipped\r\n  toolbox: distrobox 'ultramarine-44' from registry.fedoraproject.org/fedora-toolbox:44\r\n\r\n  kernel : this system runs kernel-surface 7.2.11-1.surface.fc44.x86_64 (from linux-surface); the target ships kernel 7.2.5-200.fc44.x86_64\r\n           kept: rpm-ostree override, replayed at every update\r\n           install  kernel-surface (7.2.11-1.surface.fc44)  kernel-surface-core  kernel-surface-modules  kernel-surface-modules-core  kernel-surface-modules-extra\r\n           with     iptsd  libwacom-surface  libwacom-surface-data\r\n           remove   kernel  kernel-core  kernel-devel-matched  kernel-modules  kernel-modules-core  kernel-modules-extra\r\n                    kmod-v4l2loopback  kmod-zfs  v4l2loopback  zfs\r\n\u001b[1;33mwarning:\u001b[0m kmod-v4l2loopback is removed with the target's kernel: module built for the target's kernel 7.2.5-200.fc44.x86_64\r\n\u001b[1;33mwarning:\u001b[0m kmod-zfs is removed with the target's kernel: module built for the target's kernel 7.2.5-200.fc44.x86_64\r\n\u001b[1;33mwarning:\u001b[0m v4l2loopback is removed with the target's kernel: needs v4l2loopback-kmod >= 0.15.4\r\n\u001b[1;33mwarning:\u001b[0m zfs is removed with the target's kernel: needs zfs-kmod = 2.4.4\r\n           not carried: kernel-surface-default-watchdog — built with the kernel for systems whose package manager writes boot entries; ostree writes its own\r\n           note: also installed, as the target ships its counterpart: kernel-surface-modules-extra\r\n\r\n"]
